# Controls what a `vercel` CLI deploy uploads. Two jobs:
#
#   1. lib/generated/build-info.json (gitignored, written by scripts/predeploy.mjs) MUST upload —
#      it is how /api/version knows which commit the deployment serves. Do not exclude lib/generated.
#   2. The CLI's default exclusion list is fixed (node_modules, .next, .env.local, ...) and does NOT
#      apply .gitignore patterns, so private/dev files this repo gitignores are excluded here
#      explicitly or they would ship with the source upload.
.env*
!.env.example
*.pem
logs
coverage
screenshots
*.log
*.tsbuildinfo
# Raw captures never upload; the redacted dataset/captured.public.jsonl (from
# `npm run capture:publish`) deliberately DOES ship — it is how the deployed
# /methods page renders the headline-eligible rows without the personal data.
dataset/captured.jsonl
bench/tau2/.cache
.venv
__pycache__
.DS_Store
